    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (78.06) stands as our premier offensive anchor, fueled by a favorable matchup against the mid-rotation arm of Martinez. While the platoon dynamics are slightly negative, his elite floor and the critical #2 spot in the order make him our highest-scoring start. **Jonathan Aranda** (68.87) also projects as a strong play; facing Armstrong (4.35 xERA), he benefits significantly from his position in the top third of the order and a dynamic platoon advantage against the right-handed pitcher, which elevates his base projection into a reliable start. \n\nThe bench remains stagnant today, as a league-wide off-day for the core of our roster\u2014including **Cal Raleigh**, **Bryce Harper**, **Will Smith**, and **Lawrence Butler**\u2014simplifies our decision-making process by effectively eliminating any optimization conflict. Because these high-impact contributors are inactive, we are relying on our depth pieces to maintain our 5x5 Roto standing. While **Justin Crawford**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Tyler Freeman** remain part of our long-term strategy to capture the scarcest category\u2014stolen bases\u2014they are not in active contention for points today.\n\nLooking ahead, we must be mindful of the volatility inherent in our current active starters. While **Yainer Diaz**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Dylan Beavers** are monitored, our focus remains on the matchup-specific leverage provided by **Gleyber Torres**, **Zack Gelof**, and **Luis Arraez**. We are also keeping tabs on **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, and **JJ Bleday** to ensure they capitalize on their respective environments. With **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Braden Montgomery** providing situational coverage, we are positioned to weather the slate, though the lack of elite-tier starters on the board today increases the reliance on **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Jonathan Aranda** to drive our daily category efficiency.",
